From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patryk Kowalczyk <papyszoo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:12:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: BetterVR's rumbles and the game's are one Vibration
 page, one mixer

Nine categories (swings, bow, shield/guard, gear/inventory, attacks/items/throws, runes,
the game's own rumble, damage taken, explosions), each with an on/off, a strength and the
devices it is felt on (the Sense controllers, the PS VR2 headset's motor, the DualSense).
The defaults are v0.5.0's output: every category on at 100% on the Sense controllers, the
game's pattern on both hands at full strength; the two new ones start on for the hands and
the headset. Everything lives in BetterVR_settings.ini and on the new Vibration page.

RumbleManager is a 60 Hz mixer: the game's pattern is a level per tick and each input
rumble an enveloped level on its hand, and a device gets the louder of the categories that
were switched on for it. The game pattern and BetterVR's own rumbles no longer cut each
other off. The headset and the DualSense are reached through the runtime's two sinks; while
a VR session runs Cemu's own rumble output is held back so the pad cannot fire twice. The
page has a test button for each device, and its [vib] lines say what answered.

The game's own rumble also logs, at most 40 lines 150 ms apart, the caller and, when the
sead addon is reachable, its pattern string (+0x14), so one console run can tell which
situations make which pattern.
